{"id":"CH04","time_range":"2:55-4:05","questions":["Q8"],"function":"把普通观众人化，给食物考据细节，并预告即将发生的集体活动","purpose":"제1급. Strangers become people: you swap origins with your row, meet the woman who will later guide you (an invented character), notice what gets nibbled around here, and learn why heads keep turning toward the emperor.","information_goal":"A Roman poet's account of spectators from distant peoples, flagged as one writer's praise poem (F30); fig, grape, olive and nut remains plus bear and big-cat bones from drain clearing, which reflect long use and cannot be dated to the opening year (F25); the coming ball toss, announced without showing it (F06). The neighbour is part of the invented story (F32).","emotion_goal":"Warm curiosity turning into shared anticipation","retention_goal":"Named origins and a snack detail make the crowd feel real, and the promise of the toss makes viewers wait for it.","word_budget":164,"open_loop":{"open":"LOOP06: the balls are about to be thrown; who will get the good one?","close":""},"originality_constraint":"邻座人物与对话须原创，不得沿用原视频配角的身世、梦想和用词。","locks":["LOOP06-open"],"carries_peaks":[],"fact_ids":["F30","F25"],"recap_ids":["F06","F32"],"source_segments":["FS06"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"承接底层社会生态；史料对普通观众着墨少，缩短原片这一大段，把时间留给后面的证据章节。","level_focus":"人际","level_new_info":"Who shares the top tier with you, according to a poet, and what the drains later yielded (F30, F25).","answers_prev":"挤在你身边的是些什么人，他们在盼什么？","new_lens":"The crowd is described as coming from far-off lands, and drain finds hint at what spectators ate over the years.","leaves_question":"木球扔下来的那一刻，看台会变成什么样？","step":"为什么","claim":"身边是远近各地的看客，大家眼下盼的是皇帝抛球。","ideas_new":["观众来自远方","遗存不能定年"],"reuses":[],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"挤进一排人里，认识邻座女人，你怕口音和举止露馅","words":55},{"kind":"事实数据","task":"诗人笔下的远方来客，并点明是一人的称颂诗","words":38},{"kind":"事实数据","task":"果实坚果遗存和兽骨，不能定到开幕年","words":40},{"kind":"过渡","task":"全排人突然抬头等木球","words":31}],"material":"够","cases":["迟到观众诗人"]},

{"id":"CH05","time_range":"4:05-5:20","questions":["Q9","Q10"],"function":"集体高光，收束上一章活动悬念，配角起疑并发出私下谈话邀约","purpose":"제1급. A little wooden ball is already in the air. Arms shoot up, you grab hopelessly and miss, and nobody cares. Only when your neighbour presses one into your palm does the fun stop: she has caught something odd about you and wants an explanation in private.","information_goal":"Inscribed wooden balls thrown from above and exchangeable for food, clothing, gold and silver vessels, horses, cattle and even slaves, first sourced to a historian writing more than a century later (F06); deliver the slave prize without jokes. A passing mention of a gladiator pair the crowd is eager for, with no result (F26). The neighbour's suspicion is invented (F32).","emotion_goal":"Wild communal joy, a sudden chill at one prize, then personal alarm","retention_goal":"The promised scramble pays off, and the moment you win something your cover starts to slip.","word_budget":176,"open_loop":{"open":"LOOP05: your neighbour wants a private word about who you are.","close":"LOOP06: the toss happens and a ball ends up with you through her help."},"originality_constraint":"抢球场面和邀约台词须原创，不得沿用原视频的舞会式表达、调侃和配角口吻。","locks":["LOOP06-close","PK03","LOOP05-open"],"carries_peaks":["PK03"],"fact_ids":["F06"],"recap_ids":["F26","F32"],"source_segments":["FS07"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"承接集体高光，两个连续问题一气讲完；开场直接从球飞下来起笔，坦白本身放到下一章开头，让起疑和坦白紧接。","level_focus":"转折事件","level_new_info":"What the balls could be exchanged for, including people (F06).","answers_prev":"木球扔下来的那一刻，看台会变成什么样？","new_lens":"A tiny wooden ball could be worth a meal, a horse or another human being.","leaves_question":"跟她说实话，会害了你还是帮到你？","step":"风险","claim":"抛球让看台大乱，奖品里甚至有奴隶；你拿到一颗，也引起了怀疑。","ideas_new":["奖品里包括人"],"reuses":[{"idea":"观众来自远方","from":"CH04","use":"让来处不同的人在抢球时显出同一种狂热"}],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"从球在半空起笔，众人扑抢，你什么也抓不到","words":50},{"kind":"事实数据","task":"史家记的兑换物清单与出处","words":38},{"kind":"观点判断","task":"念到奴隶时收住笑","words":22},{"kind":"经营场景","task":"邻座帮你拿到球，顺口提起大家盼的两名角斗士","words":36},{"kind":"过渡","task":"她压低声音要你私下说清来历","words":30}],"material":"够","cases":["百年后的记录者","打平的两个人"]},

{"id":"CH06","time_range":"5:20-6:40","questions":["Q11"],"function":"向配角坦白身份换取路线情报，限时伪装完成层级突破","purpose":"제1급. In a quiet corner you confess that you come from the future. Instead of reporting you, she trades you a way down and a brief window. Aged 26, with the ball still in your hand, you shed the dark cloak, bluff past the people who could stop you, and finish at the edge of the senators' area as an intruder with no rightful seat.","information_goal":"The seating rule that makes the move risky, as an Augustan rule applied to this arena by inference (F16); the confession, route, window and disguise are invented, as declared at the start (F32).","emotion_goal":"Playful suspense tightening into real fear of exposure","retention_goal":"A risky truth buys a route with a time limit, and each step down could end with you being thrown out.","word_budget":187,"open_loop":{"open":"","close":"LOOP02: you reach the area near the field."},"originality_constraint":"坦白对话、路线与伪装方式须原创，不得沿用原视频的坦白对象设定、通道和道别方式。","locks":["LOOP02-close"],"carries_peaks":[],"fact_ids":["F16"],"recap_ids":["F32","F17"],"source_segments":["FS08"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"承接坦白加潜入；单独成章给足过程，让层级突破有代价、有紧张感。到达场边和手里有什么在本章交代完，下一章直接看。","level_focus":"风险","level_new_info":"The dress and seating rule is now the thing you must fake your way past (F16).","answers_prev":"跟她说实话，会害了你还是帮到你？","new_lens":"Telling the truth gets you a route, but only for a short while and only under a false appearance.","leaves_question":"前排和楼上到底差多少？","step":"成本和限制","claim":"坦白换来了下到场边的机会，但时间有限，身份是装的。","ideas_new":["限时的通行机会"],"reuses":[{"idea":"身份决定离场地多远","from":"CH01","use":"这次变成要绕过的实际障碍"}],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"角落里坦白，她的反应","words":55},{"kind":"商业解释","task":"为什么下不去：深色斗篷与女性座位的规定","words":32},{"kind":"经营场景","task":"路线、时间窗、换下斗篷","words":50},{"kind":"经营场景","task":"一路下行险些被问住，站到场边","words":38},{"kind":"过渡","task":"眼前的座位和楼上完全两样","words":12}],"material":"够","cases":[]},

{"id":"CH07","time_range":"6:40-7:55","questions":["Q12"],"function":"禁区奇观与阶层硬对照，中点观众自测，埋下脚下这层地面的疑问","purpose":"제2급. Not daring to sit, you size up the senators' places against the bench you had upstairs. Cranes fight, then four elephants, close enough to unsettle you. Your eyes drop to the sand, and you ask the viewer to guess what will happen to it.","information_goal":"A priestly brotherhood's allotted seating length cut in stone, about 37 meters by modern reading (F20); a plank floor covered in sand with space below (F23); crane fights and a contest of four elephants, with their placement in this day treated as reconstruction (F07). One line recalling that the nearest seats were for senators (F16).","emotion_goal":"Awe mixed with the sting of inequality","retention_goal":"The viewer finally sees the sand at close range and is asked to guess its fate before the story answers.","word_budget":176,"open_loop":{"open":"","close":""},"originality_constraint":"奇观描写与观众自测的句子须原创，不得沿用原视频对上层空间的惊叹方式和比喻。","locks":["PK04"],"carries_peaks":["PK04"],"fact_ids":["F20","F23","F07"],"recap_ids":["F16","F17"],"source_segments":["FS09"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"承接禁区奇观；到达过程上一章已讲完，这里直接从观察开始。中点换成观众自测，两名角斗士的结局留到后面。","level_focus":"规则","level_new_info":"Rank is literally measured and written in stone, and from here the floor reads as boards, sand and a hidden space (F20, F23).","answers_prev":"前排和楼上到底差多少？","new_lens":"Some groups had their seat space recorded in stone, and the sand is only a layer over boards with space underneath.","leaves_question":"这场庆典还能夸张到什么地步？","step":"有多少(算账)","claim":"前排连座位长度都有记录，而脚下沙地下面还有空间。","ideas_new":["座位长度刻在石头上","沙下有空间"],"reuses":[{"idea":"顶层的距离感","from":"CH03","use":"和场边视角直接对比"}],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"不敢落座，从场边打量元老的位置","words":30},{"kind":"对比案例","task":"元老席与顶层的差别，祭司团座位石刻","words":48},{"kind":"经营场景","task":"鹤相斗、四象相斗，旁人习以为常","words":42},{"kind":"事实数据","task":"木板铺沙与下方空间","words":26},{"kind":"观点判断","task":"让观众猜这层地面接下来会怎样","words":30}],"material":"够","cases":[]},

{"id":"CH10","time_range":"9:40-10:55","questions":["Q16"],"function":"把反对证据和支持理由逐一正面摆出，同时彩排要说的话","purpose":"제2급. Before risking your cover, you test the account in your head while rehearsing what to say. You conclude only that the flooding may have happened: there are reasons to doubt it and an argument that it was possible. And leaving to warn him may make you miss what you came to check.","information_goal":"Dio wrote late (F04); Suetonius places Titus's mock sea battle at an old naval basin (F08); the poet's show poems have an uncertain date and occasion (F11); one 2007 engineering study argues that filling may have been feasible, with a plaster-lined underground and a possible aqueduct branch, while no archaeological evidence shows how supply reached the arena or was controlled (F12); modern estimates run from about half an hour to several hours, which sits awkwardly with the word suddenly (F13); scholarly doubts about pipes and size, with a suggestion that purpose-built small boats may have been used (F14); disagreement over the underfloor structure at the opening (F02).","emotion_goal":"Focused, uneasy determination","retention_goal":"Viewers weigh the case for and against while the window for your warning keeps shrinking.","word_budget":176,"open_loop":{"open":"","close":""},"originality_constraint":"","locks":[],"carries_peaks":[],"fact_ids":["F08","F11","F12","F13","F14","F02"],"recap_ids":["F04"],"source_segments":["FS12"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"反方证据集中在中后段一次讲清，诗的年代疑问和耗时推算也在这里第一次交代；不让主角钻到场地下面，因为当时构造本身有分歧。","level_focus":"规则","level_new_info":"The other Roman writer's different location and the missing supply evidence (F08, F12).","answers_prev":"动手之前先想清楚，那条注水的记载靠得住吗？","new_lens":"The doubts are concrete: another writer names a different place, no supply route has been proven, and filling would not have been instant.","leaves_question":"你的警告，皇帝那边的人听得进去吗？","step":"成本和限制","claim":"有说法认为注水可行，开幕海战可能发生过，但疑点实在，不能当定论。","ideas_new":["另一史家记在别处","供水线路缺考古证据","工程上可能可行","注水耗时的推算范围"],"reuses":[{"idea":"开幕注水海战的记载","from":"CH08","use":"这次逐条检验它"},{"idea":"沙下有空间","from":"CH07","use":"拿来讨论下面能不能盛水"}],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"一边往皇帝那头挪，一边在心里过说辞和疑点","words":28},{"kind":"对比案例","task":"两位史家写法不同，诗的年代场合也存疑","words":42},{"kind":"商业解释","task":"工程研究认为可能可行、供水证据缺口、耗时推算、学者怀疑","words":65},{"kind":"事实数据","task":"地下结构的分歧","words":20},{"kind":"过渡","task":"去提醒就可能错过那一幕，你还是去了","words":21}],"material":"缩小:原来要回答注水记载靠不靠得住，现在只回答它有哪些疑点、为什么仍可能发生","cases":["百年后的记录者"]},

{"id":"CH12","time_range":"11:30-12:30","questions":["Q19"],"function":"按进程呈现场面发生，旁观者的轻松反衬知情者的沉重，回收沙地埋点","purpose":"제2급. Back at the edge, you watch one possible version of events unfold in this reconstructed journey: the sand darkens, water gathers, boats float and two sides fight, while your neighbour calls it just a show. Say plainly that this is how it may have looked, compressed and imagined from a disputed record.","information_goal":"The account of filling and ship battle, as one historian tells it (F04); the poet's address to latecomers that this was land just now (F10). One short callback each to the poem's uncertain occasion (F11), the range of filling time (F13), the unproven supply route (F12) and the doubts about size and boats (F14). Invented details (F32).","emotion_goal":"Overwhelming spectacle shadowed by unease","retention_goal":"The sand planted since the opening visibly changes, answering the biggest wait of the video.","word_budget":140,"open_loop":{"open":"","close":"LOOP04: in this journey's reconstruction the sand becomes water and boats fight on it, as it may have happened."},"originality_constraint":"进程描写与旁观者台词须原创，不得沿用原视频的时间戳写法和轻描淡写句。","locks":["LOOP04-close"],"carries_peaks":[],"fact_ids":["F10"],"recap_ids":["F04","F11","F12","F13","F14","F32"],"source_segments":["FS14"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"承接进程式高潮；疑点和耗时上一章已讲透，这里只一句带过，把篇幅留给画面和诗人的话。","level_focus":"转折事件","level_new_info":"A poet's words to latecomers about land turning into water (F10).","answers_prev":"那片沙地，到底有没有变成水面？","new_lens":"A poet tells latecomers not to be fooled: the water in front of them was land a moment ago.","leaves_question":"这一百天热闹下来，付出了什么，又是怎么收场的？","step":"反转","claim":"按史家和诗人的说法，沙地可能变成过水面；眼前的过程是复原想象。","ideas_new":["陆地转眼成水面"],"reuses":[{"idea":"沙下有空间","from":"CH07","use":"兑现埋点，让观众看着地面消失"},{"idea":"注水耗时的推算范围","from":"CH10","use":"说明画面为什么压缩了时间"},{"idea":"供水线路缺考古证据","from":"CH10","use":"说明画面为什么只能算复原"}],"units":[{"kind":"经营场景","task":"沙面变深、积水、船浮起开打","words":65},{"kind":"对比案例","task":"诗人提醒迟到者，邻座说不过是场表演","words":45},{"kind":"观点判断","task":"一句点明这是可能的样子，时间经过压缩","words":18},{"kind":"过渡","task":"热闹背后的代价","words":12}],"material":"缩小:原来要回答沙地有没有变成水面，现在只呈现按记载它可能是什么样","cases":["迟到观众诗人"]},

{"id":"CH13","time_range":"12:30-13:15","questions":["Q20"],"function":"呈现庆典的代价与见证者决堤，以无解的情绪事件留余韵","purpose":"제2급. Once the boats are gone, what you see is killing, and you force yourself not to look away. One mercy follows as two fighters both walk out. Then the hundred days close with the host crying in front of everyone, and you cannot tell why.","information_goal":"About 9,000 tame and wild animals killed, Dio's combined account of the theatre and baths dedication, with some women of low standing taking part (F03, F07); Priscus and Verus fought to a draw and both received the wooden sword, per one praise poem, with the order of events reconstructed (F26); Titus wept before the people at the close, cause unsettled (F27), and died the next year (F28). Do not calculate a daily average.","emotion_goal":"Grief, a brief tenderness, then a lingering unanswered feeling","retention_goal":"The story turns from spectacle to cost and to a tear no source can settle.","word_budget":105,"open_loop":{"open":"","close":""},"originality_constraint":"","locks":["PK08"],"carries_peaks":["PK08"],"fact_ids":["F03","F26","F27"],"recap_ids":["F07","F28"],"source_segments":["FS15"],"treatment":"保留功能换内容","layout_reason":"代价、一次生还、皇帝落泪依次并置，不加形容；开场直接进入表演之后看到的事。","level_focus":"代价","level_new_info":"The scale of animal deaths, the double release and the public weeping (F03, F26, F27).","answers_prev":"这一百天热闹下来，付出了什么，又是怎么收场的？","new_lens":"The celebration cost thousands of animal lives and ended with its host in tears for reasons nobody has settled.","leaves_question":"走完这一趟，你要核对的事有结果了吗：开幕只有沙地和角斗？","step":"成本和限制","claim":"盛典的代价很大，收场时提图斯当众痛哭，原因没有定论。","ideas_new":["盛典的动物代价","平手双双获释","皇帝落泪原因不明"],"reuses":[{"idea":"提醒无法改变结局","from":"CH11","use":"落泪之后再看他剩下的时间"}],"units":[{"kind":"事实数据","task":"动物被杀的合计与统计范围","words":30},{"kind":"对比案例","task":"两名角斗士同获木剑","words":28},{"kind":"经营场景","task":"你看着皇帝当众痛哭","words":35},{"kind":"过渡","task":"回头问这趟核对的结果","words":12}],"material":"够","cases":["打平的两个人","落泪的皇帝"]}
],
